# Daily capture, complete resolution

## Usage (caller’s view)

```rust
// Scheduled daily invocation; bootstrap automatically when no published snapshot exists.
let report = ingestion.synchronize(SyncRequest::Daily).await?;
// Periodic complete acquisition compares upstream with retained evidence.
let report = ingestion.synchronize(SyncRequest::Reconcile).await?;
// Retry a durable prepared run without fetching a different dataset under its ID.
let report = ingestion.resume(run_id).await?;
```

Proposed CLI: `data declarations sync`, `data declarations sync --reconcile`, and `data declarations sync --resume <run-id>`. Output identifies the run, committed generation, acquisition counts, and unresolved source discrepancies. Existing clean/resolve commands remain usable for inspecting retained artifacts.

## Problem

Reduce daily Parliament API acquisition while preserving complete identity evidence and parent attribution. Today capture fetches every stored member; the loader safely retries exact runs but preserves omitted declarations. Noncompany identities depend on the ingestion run, aliases depend on supplied evidence, and parents can affect unchanged children. A small input cannot safely be treated as a small independent resolution problem.

## Shape

Recommend **incremental acquisition into immutable complete snapshots, followed by existing global clean/resolve and one complete publication**. Initially use change discovery to select members, then reacquire all interests for each selected member. This costs more than individual-interest fetches but keeps version selection, parent context, and source responses aligned with existing behavior.

Daily discovery unions inclusive Published and Updated windows, deduplicates member IDs, and includes newly stored members. Fix an upper cutoff at run start and overlap the previous committed checkpoint. These are bounded scans, not a claimed reliable changefeed. Retain discovery pages for audit. A live probe returned one version for a date-filtered interest but two without date filters: filtered results are discovery only; hydrate with the unfiltered member fetch. Do not advance discovery state until publication commits.

```rust
